{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `partOffset` re-walk makes the hard-cut path O(n²) for non-ASCII runs — a regression vs the old O(n) per-token walk, and the new regression guard cannot see it**

`writeRunSliced` slices a long same-width run across rows, but each slice recomputes `partOffset(part, from)` and `partOffset(part, from + take)` by walking **from rune 0** every time. For an ASCII part the `ascii` fast path is O(1), but any non-ASCII run (CJK, emoji/surrogate pairs — `runAscii == false`) pays O(from) per slice, i.e. O(n²/width) for one hard-cut word. Measured on this branch (warm VM):

```
CJK single word 10000 runes:  16ms
CJK single word 20000 runes:  21ms
CJK single word 40000 runes:  79ms   (~4x per doubling = quadratic)
CJK single word 80000 runes: 292ms
```

The old per-char tokenizer was linear here (~164ms per 1M CJK *cells*, i.e. ~50ms per 80K runes), so for long unbroken non-ASCII tokens this rewrite is **slower than the code it replaced** — extrapolating the measured curve, a 1M-rune (2 MB) unbroken CJK/emoji token hard-cuts in tens of seconds. That is squarely in the PR's own threat model ("transcript bursts are single multi-100KB lines").

The regression guard misses it by construction: `cjkProse` inserts a space every 17 runes (words are 34 cells < width 80, so `writeRunSliced` never runs on CJK), and the hard-cut growth test (`oneGiantWord`) is pure ASCII, which only exercises the O(1) `ascii` offset path.

The fix is cheap — the slices are sequential and `from` is monotonic, so carry the unit offset incrementally instead of re-walking:

```dart
void writeRunSliced(_WrapPart part) {
  final w = part.runeWidth;
  var from = 0;
  var unitFrom = 0; // char offset of `from`, advanced incrementally
  while (from < part.runes) {
    if (col > 0 && col + w > width) closeRow();
    final cap = col == 0 ? (w > width ? 1 : width ~/ w) : (width - col) ~/ w;
    if (cap <= 0) continue;
    final take = cap < part.runes - from ? cap : part.runes - from;
    final start = unitFrom;
    final end = unitFrom = partOffsetFrom(part, unitFrom, from, take);
    row.write(part.text.substring(start, end));
    col += take * w;
    from += take;
  }
}
```

(or precompute the rune→unit offsets once per non-ASCII part). Byte output is unchanged either way, and it would also be worth adding a long-CJK-single-word case to the growth contract so this path is actually gated.
